<!--
  CNC.Svg - SVG artwork to contours, and contours to laser g-code, with NO WPF and no native
  dependencies, so the same assembly runs under .NET on a Raspberry Pi as under .NET Framework
  inside ioSender.

  WHY IT EXISTS: SvgOutlines used to live in CNC Controls because it leaned on WPF's Geometry.Parse
  and GetFlattenedPathGeometry. PresentationCore is Windows-only, which meant the SVG-to-laser
  converter could not run on the EngravingBox appliance that ultimately burns the file. Extracting
  it needed exactly one thing replaced - the path parser and flattener (SvgPath.cs) plus the affine
  matrix it used (SvgMatrix.cs). Everything else was already portable arithmetic.

  Nothing in here may reference WPF, System.Drawing, or any native library. The point of the
  assembly is that EngravingBox can xcopy it; a per-architecture .so would defeat that. The
  net8 portability probe (CNC.Svg.net8.csproj, same folder, same sources, NOT in the .sln) is what
  keeps that honest - it fails the moment a Windows-only reference creeps in.

  This is the LEGACY net462 project the solution builds - same two-project pattern as CNC Common,
  CNC Core and CNC Contracts.
-->
